## Importing Existing Resources

All Dokploy resources support importing via `terraform import`. This allows you to bring existing Dokploy infrastructure under Terraform management.

### Import Workflow

#### Step 1: Discover Resource IDs

Use the data sources to discover existing resource IDs:

```hcl
# Discover all projects and their IDs
data "dokploy_projects" "all" {}

output "project_ids" {
  value = { for p in data.dokploy_projects.all.projects : p.name => p.id }
}

# Discover environments within a project
data "dokploy_environments" "all" {
  project_id = "your-project-id"
}

output "environment_ids" {
  value = { for e in data.dokploy_environments.all.environments : e.name => e.id }
}
```

Run `terraform apply` to see the IDs:

```bash
terraform apply -target=data.dokploy_projects.all
```

#### Step 2: Create Import Blocks (Terraform 1.5+)

Using the discovered IDs, create import blocks:

```hcl
import {
  to = dokploy_project.existing
  id = "abc123-project-id"
}

import {
  to = dokploy_environment.prod
  id = "def456-environment-id"
}
```

#### Step 3: Generate Configuration

Use Terraform to generate the resource configuration:

```bash
terraform plan -generate-config-out=generated.tf
```

#### Step 4: Import Resources

```bash
terraform apply
```

### Classic Import Command

For Terraform versions before 1.5, use the import command:

```bash
terraform import dokploy_project.existing abc123-project-id
terraform import dokploy_environment.prod def456-environment-id
```

### Import Helper Script

A helper script is available to generate import blocks for all existing resources:

```bash
# Set environment variables
export DOKPLOY_HOST="https://your-dokploy-instance.com"
export DOKPLOY_API_KEY="your-api-key"

# Generate import blocks
./scripts/dokploy-import.sh > imports.tf

# Generate configuration
terraform plan -generate-config-out=generated.tf
```

### Available Data Sources for Discovery

| Data Source | Description |
|-------------|-------------|
| `dokploy_projects` | List all projects |
| `dokploy_environments` | List environments in a project (includes applications, databases) |
| `dokploy_servers` | List all servers |
| `dokploy_ssh_keys` | List all SSH keys |
| `dokploy_registries` | List all container registries |
| `dokploy_certificates` | List all SSL certificates |
| `dokploy_destinations` | List all backup destinations |

## Authentication

The provider supports authentication via API key:

```hcl
provider "dokploy" {
  host    = "https://your-dokploy-instance.com"
  api_key = var.dokploy_api_key
}
```

Or via environment variables:

```bash
export DOKPLOY_HOST="https://your-dokploy-instance.com"
export DOKPLOY_API_KEY="your-api-key"
```
